  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: CommAddDisc 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "During a virtual Q&A session hosted by a cancer center, a research team
    shares that they are exploring new targets \u2014 a specific part of cancer that
    researchers focus on when developing new treatments \u2014 to pursue in their
    early discovery experiments. A volunteer from the research center encourages
    virtual attendees to give feedback, explaining, \u201CCommunity advocates can
    help build trust and transparency between the research team and the patient community,
    even in the early discovery stage of research.\u201D\n\nIs this true or false?"
  explanation: 'Involving community advocates early helps researchers stay connected
    to patient needs and ensures the community understands why and how the research
    is happening. This early engagement builds trust and prepares the way for future
    studies. By sharing their perspectives and asking questions, community advocates
    help make the research process more transparent and meaningful for cancer patients
    and families. '
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
